# Applied ON TOP of .env by `make load-test` (docker compose --env-file .env --env-file .env.loadtest).
# Only the gateway's per-IP rate limits change, and only for the duration of the test:
# k6 sends every request from one IP, so the production limits (100/min, 10/min for
# auth) would turn ~99% of the run into 429s and measure nothing else.
#
# The limiter stays IN the request path (Redis Lua sliding window) so its cost is
# still part of the latency being measured; the ceilings are just unreachable.
# Redis memory for the limiter ~ requests per window * ~100 B (a few tens of MB here).
RATE_LIMIT_REQUESTS=100000000
RATE_LIMIT_WINDOW=1m
AUTH_RATE_LIMIT_REQUESTS=100000000
AUTH_RATE_LIMIT_WINDOW=1m
LOG_LEVEL=warn
